# =============================================================================
#  assets/textures/farm_path.pix  —  the sixteen path pieces the pack did not have
# =============================================================================
#  Kenney's Tiny Town has a nine-piece dirt PATCH: the pieces you need to fill an
#  area. The farm's path is one tile wide, which is a LINE, and a line needs the
#  other set — two ends, four elbows, four T-junctions, a crossroads. No pack in
#  hand ships them and no amount of noise generates them, so they are drawn here.
#
#  The shapes are ours. The three colours are Kenney's own dirt, sampled from
#  `town.hrt` tile 40 (CC0, no obligation), so the path sits INSIDE the pack's
#  palette instead of next to it — see assets/ATTRIBUTION.md.
#
#  THE TILE INDEX IS THE NEIGHBOUR MASK. north=1, east=2, south=4, west=8, so tile
#  5 is north|south (a vertical run) and tile 15 is all four. That is not a
#  convenience: it is what lets `farm::path_piece` be a bit shuffle instead of a
#  lookup table nobody can check, and it makes this file readable in grid order.
#
#  Every piece is the same corridor: cols/rows 3..12, ten of sixteen. An arm runs
#  from the centre block to the tile edge on each connected side, and the outer
#  corners stay grass — that is why a one-wide path looks like a path and not like
#  a chain of squares. The dark pixels are the edge of the corridor, and they are
#  computed from the shape rather than decided per piece, which is what makes the
#  seams line up: two connected tiles meet with no dark line between them, and
#  `test_farm` checks exactly that.
#
#  Re-bake after editing (the committed .hrt must be what this file says):
#      ./build/demo --cmd asset.pixels textures/farm_path.pix textures/farm_path.hrt
# =============================================================================

size 16
grid 4 4

palette . 00000000     # grass shows through
palette d eaa56c       # Kenney dirt
palette D cf8254       # ...its shadow, used for the corridor edge
palette l fec99c       # ...its highlight, three specks so the fill is not flat

tile 0                 # nothing attached
................
................
................
